From 7cb807ac55f58bfb6110bf064013bd9723b0dbe4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian MacDonald <ian@netstatz.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 23:44:41 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 109/109] docs: the image route spec names every probe refusal

The /v1/images/classify note said an executorch or onnxruntime load fails
only when the engine has no POST /classify/image route; it also fails when
the probe gets a 2xx, a 5xx, a timeout or a crash. The Inspection comment
now says what from_files skips: only a dir with no manifest declaring the
image task and not both tokenizer.json and config.json. The API reference
is regenerated.

Assisted-by: claude:opus-5.5
---
 docs/api/lemonade.md                                        | 2 +-
 src/cpp/include/lemon/backends/classifier_backend.h         | 6 ++++--
 .../server/routes/lemonade/inference/images_classify.cpp    | 6 ++++--
 3 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/api/lemonade.md b/docs/api/lemonade.md
index 0c3f7e362..46a2bf4a4 100644
--- a/docs/api/lemonade.md
+++ b/docs/api/lemonade.md
@@ -192,7 +192,7 @@ An image model directory holds the graph (`model.tflite` for `tflite`, `model.pt
 
 `"layout": "auto"` (the same as `"NHWC"`) expects an input of `[1, H, W, 3]`; a PyTorch export (`[1, 3, H, W]`), as `et-server` and `ort-server` usually load, sets `"NCHW"`, and an input that does not match the declared layout is refused at load. A text model directory (the graph + `tokenizer.json` + `config.json`, with no `manifest.json` declaring the image-classification task) is served by `/v1/classify`.
 
-`manifest.json` must resolve inside the model directory (or inside its repository for a downloaded snapshot), be a regular file of at most 1 MiB and hold a JSON object; the labels file must resolve the same way. A directory whose manifest or labels file fails a check is not served, for text models too: the model stays registered, loading it fails with the reason, and the server log names the directory once in a warning. Loading also fails with a message naming both layouts when a model's label and its directory disagree; for `tflite`, when the installed `tflite-server` is too old to report the image-classification task; and for `executorch` and `onnxruntime`, when the engine has no `POST /classify/image` route. The per-model `tflite_args`, `executorch_args` or `onnxruntime_args` option passes flags such as `--max-image-pixels` through to the engine.
+`manifest.json` must resolve inside the model directory (or inside its repository for a downloaded snapshot), be a regular file of at most 1 MiB and hold a JSON object; the labels file must resolve the same way. A directory whose manifest or labels file fails a check is not served, for text models too: the model stays registered, loading it fails with the reason, and the server log names the directory once in a warning. Loading also fails with a message naming both layouts when a model's label and its directory disagree; for `tflite`, when the installed `tflite-server` is too old to report the image-classification task; and for `executorch` and `onnxruntime`, when the load probe (an image request without an image) does not confirm the engine's `POST /classify/image` route: the engine has none, or the probe gets a 2xx, a 5xx, a timeout or a crash. The per-model `tflite_args`, `executorch_args` or `onnxruntime_args` option passes flags such as `--max-image-pixels` through to the engine.
 
 ### Example
 
diff --git a/src/cpp/include/lemon/backends/classifier_backend.h b/src/cpp/include/lemon/backends/classifier_backend.h
index 7e01b7edc..4b3991895 100644
--- a/src/cpp/include/lemon/backends/classifier_backend.h
+++ b/src/cpp/include/lemon/backends/classifier_backend.h
@@ -30,8 +30,10 @@ enum class Layout { None, Text, Image };
 struct Inspection {
     Layout layout;
     std::string problem;
-    // False when the dir merely lacks layout files (a stray or partly downloaded
-    // graph): that is not logged or listed as a refusal.
+    // False when the only problem is missing layout files: no manifest.json
+    // declaring the image task, and not both tokenizer.json and config.json (a
+    // stray graph, or a text model still downloading). That is not logged or
+    // listed as a refusal; manifest and labels failures are.
     bool from_files = true;
 };
 
